+## Company artifact catalog
+
+Declare `artifacts.read` to read the same company-scoped catalog used by the native Artifacts page:
+
+```ts
+const page = await ctx.artifacts.list({
+  companyId,
+  kind: "image",
+  projectId,
+  q: "launch",
+  limit: 100,
+  cursor: previousPage?.nextCursor ?? undefined,
+});
+```
+
+`PluginArtifactsListInput` accepts `kind`, `projectId`, `q`, `groupBy` (`none`, `task`, `parent_task`), `groupIssueId`, `limit` (1–100), and the opaque `cursor`. The response is `CompanyArtifactsResponse`: `artifacts`, `nextCursor`, and optional `groups`/`selectedGroup` for grouped queries. Call it from a company-scoped UI, API, tool, or event invocation; a missing, expired, or different host-authorized company scope is denied before querying. The worker and host both enforce `artifacts.read`.
+
+Native per-user `starred` filtering is excluded. Store plugin folders, tags, favorites, and saved views in plugin-owned company metadata. The host delegates to the canonical artifact service, preserving document/attachment/work-product classification, deduplication, hidden-task exclusion, filter validation, and cursor pagination. No artifact source is copied or mutated. Unit fixtures may be seeded with `harness.seed({ artifacts: [{ companyId, ...artifact }] })`.
